ncMock(return_value=None)\n        response = client.get(\"/api/queries/nonexistent-id\")\n    assert response.status_code == 404\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Gaps\n\n| Module | Tested | Key Untested Areas |\n|---|---|---|\n| `llm/client.py` | 0% | init, retry, streaming, JSON parse error |\n| `fetch/engine.py` | ~5% | normalize URL, domain extract, cache fallback, `FetchError` |\n| `fetch/cache.py` | 0% | TTL logic, `is_valid`, domain TTL selection |\n| `fetch/extractors.py` | ~20% | truncate, fallback selector, heading format, exception path |\n| `agents/orchestrator.py` | 0% | synthesis, routing fallback, citation dedup, streaming |\n| `agents/specialist.py` | 0% | parse response, build context, fetch failure accounting |\n| `data/db.py` | ~15% | agent responses, orchestrator responses, feedback, cache CRUD |\n| `api/websocket.py` | 0% | manager send/disconnect/broadcast, `process_query` flow |\n| `api/routes.py` | 0% | all endpoints |\n\nThe highest-risk untested paths are the **JSON parse fallback branches** in both orchestrator and specialist (these are the silent-failure paths), the **GeminiClient retry logic**, and the **FetchEngine stale-cache fallback** — all three are the exact places that will misbehave silently in production under real network or LLM errors.\n",
